## AI-assisted authorship

A substantial part of this codebase — the majority of the feature pull
requests numbered #2 through #64 — was produced with the assistance of an
AI coding agent (`arena-ai-coding-agent`, also committing as
`Arena Agent <agent@arena.ai>`) running in Arena.ai's Agent Mode.

The AI agent is a tool, not a legal person. It holds no copyright, it is
not a contributor for licensing purposes, and it grants no licence. Every
change it produced was:

- initiated by the copyright holder, from prompts and specifications the
  copyright holder wrote;
- directed, reviewed, corrected, and iterated on by the copyright holder;
- accepted or rejected solely at the copyright holder's discretion, and
  merged into the default branch only by the copyright holder (see, for
  example, the revert of PR #63 in PR #64);
- integrated into the copyright holder's own selection, arrangement, and
  architecture of the work as a whole.

The copyright holder therefore asserts ownership of the resulting work and
of the rights necessary to license it, including the right to release it
under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any
later version.

To the extent that any individual machine-generated fragment is held not to
attract copyright protection, that fragment is either (a) not subject to
copyright and so freely usable by anyone, or (b) owned by the copyright
holder above; in neither case does it encumber the rights granted by this
project's licence, and no third party holds a competing claim to it.

